  abstract = {At present, EEG-based emotion recognition has advanced significantly. However, models' discrimination ability across subjects remains limited because of ignoring the electrode structure and the cross-subject differences in EEG signals. To address this, we propose a discrimination-enhanced hierarchical network with structure optimization (SO-DHNet), a discrimination-enhanced hierarchical network with structure optimization for cross-subject EEG emotion recognition. It includes a hierarchical data generation (HDG) module that organizes EEG electrodes into five neuroanatomical regions, optimizes their structure, and generates 4D hierarchical data. Additionally, we introduce a random pairing training (RPT) strategy with a pairwise-similarity binary cross-entropy (PS-BCE) loss to maximize inter-class diversity and minimize intra-class variability. Experiments on SEED confirm SO-DHNet's effectiveness in cross-subject emotion recognition.},
}

